times played  in the Maracana but not more than one  per week for the bars few customers  there's just one topic of conversation  first they let the public pay the huge  price tag then they simply close the  doors that's not right we paid for this  Stadium with our taxes wasn't cheap  we're still paying it off we have a lot  of problems in the city this wallet  stadium is simply a microcosm of the  bigger crisis we're facing in Rio the  stadium's fortunes may be shifting to  interested parties want to take over the  contract and get the Maracana back in  shape so perhaps this gloomy phase is  just a sad chapter in a bigger story  that will have a happier ending few  Brazilians see their countries bigger  crises in the same way
 

